    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0966" n="862" xml:id="pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.05/46</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ethiopia (Southard) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1272</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-26">October 26,
                        1933</date>.<lb/>[Received November 22.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Legation’s No. 1264 of October 17, 1933, forwarding a draft of the Diplomatic
                    Corps proposal for reorganization and reform of the Special Tribunal (Mixed
                    Court).</p>
                <p>As stated in our No. 1264 each local Legation sent this proposal to its
                    Government for approval or instruction. My British colleague has obtained by
                    telegraph his Government’s approval and comment, which he outlines in a letter
                    of October 19, 1933, to each local Legation. A copy of the letter is herewith
                    enclosed for the information of the Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addison E. Southard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d636-a1.xml" xpointer="d636-a1"/>
